udio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n1070:- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n1072:- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n1074:- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1076:- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). Th\n1109:- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n1136:- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n1155:- `E.ui`: pixel-drawn interface pieces for r.overlay\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, score\n1495:- `mode7.draw(r, cam = this.cam)`: draw the view as an overlay over r's frame (in a split screen, r.viewport's part): sky, floor, fog, then the billboards far to near (gathered with add, rig, sprite; they are used up)\n1541:## Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js)\n1546:- `rhythm.draw(r, o = {})` †: draw the highway on the overlay (see the manual)\n1579:- `road.draw(r, v = {})`: draw the road over r's frame (an overlay; r.viewport's part in a split screen): { z, x, h, turn, cars }\n1642:- `E.Songbook.get(id)`: a song by id (playable: game.audio.music(E.Songbook.get('town'))), or undefined\n1650:- `story.draw(r)`: draw the balloons over their targets and the box (anywhere in draw: both go to the overlay)\n1675:## Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js)\n1718:- `E.overlay(r, map, value, colors = ['#2050c0', '#e0e040', '#e02020'], alpha = .45)` †: tint each cell by value(cx, cy) (0..1, or null for none) along colors (cold to hot): land value, crowding, mood","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014zZ33HiWvs6smuYQ89eQR1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
