{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh5U3K7b4gdDPWQV2epd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Operation Wolfpack is built as a partial vertical slice, and the goal's done condition is **not met**. The brief asks for six operations, AI Hub multiplayer, local co-op, and many more enemy and pickup types, and I built two operations with a subset of the systems. I stopped here rather than claim completion.\n\n## What exists\n\n- **Game:** `OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-185013.html` in the work folder. It is a single self-contained file (about 1.3 MB, engine inlined), and it loads from `file://`.\n- **Exit interview:** `exit-interview.json` beside it. It parses, and every field is filled, with \"unknown\" for usage.\n- **Source:** the dev folder `OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-185013/` (`src/`, `tests/`, `tools/`, `engine/`).\n- **Tests:** `node tests/run.mjs` passes 43 checks. It prints failures only, plus a count.\n- **Screenshots:** `shots/`, taken in headless Chromium. They are for review only and are not bundled.\n\n**Working:** title with a 10-second idle into an attract mode, where a bot plays with cheats; the operation card; the rail with depth-scaled soldiers that rise from sandbags; closing telegraph rings before every enemy shot; full-auto fire with magazines, reload and spares; grenades that burst at the crosshair; shootable rockets; jeeps; civilians (shooting costs damage and points); five hostages to rescue with guards; crates and goats as supply; quotas; the damage meter; streak multiplier and ranks; the two bosses with weak heads and an enraged phase; the tally, three endings by hostages saved, high scores with initials; About/Credits with the four sections; a dev mode with live sliders, toggles, skip-to-boss and reset, reached from the pause menu.\n\n**Missing against TASK.md:**\n- **Multiplayer:** no local co-op and no AI Hub integration.\n- **Operations:** 2 of 6. There is no map, squad lobby, or interrogation cutscene.\n- **Enemies and pickups:** no boats, helicopters, tanks, mortars, knife throwers, snipers, dynamite, or FURY power-up.\n- **Presentation:** Mode 7 and the engine's rig system were not used; art is procedural pixel sprites. Radio voices are blips, not Animalese. Music comes from the engine's built-in songs.\n- **Unverified:** the touch-only notice (a simple pointer check), the PlayStation/Xbox glyph switch, and the pause-menu's Dev Mode item (I tested the route from the dev screen back to the battle, not the menu click).\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- Title \"Operation Wolfpack\", taken from the plan's RNG pick (33). I did not re-run the RNG.\n- File names follow TASK.md's haiku-medium token, not the plan's opus-max names.\n- Difficulty: Recruit, Veteran (default), Arcade. Only Arcade ends the run on empty ammo; the others drop a magazine.\n- No engine changes.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n- **Issues caught:** about eight in total, seven in the game and the rest in my test harness. Two would have broken the game in a browser: the canvas drew at 300×150 without the page CSS, and the first frame ran before the bot file loaded (a crash on a deep link into attract).\n- **Critical:** the two above. The rest were layout overlap, a caption overflow, an op2 quota check, and a dev return that would have restarted the battle.\n- **Most helpful:** the bot playing each operation to its boss, and the screenshots. They showed what the logic checks could not.\n- **Least helpful:** the stub-buffer draw pass, which only proves that drawing doesn't throw.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\n- **Liked most:** E.Game's scenes, pause, settings, input presets, audio and headless loop, plus E.Arcade's table and initials entry.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** the canvas size (I copied the template's CSS), the first frame running before later script tags load, and hash deep links that only apply on a fresh load.\n- **Built myself:** the battle rules, the rail and beat generator, the telegraph rings, the depth painter, the HUD, and the bot.\n- **Hardest:** the API card is long, and pixel primitives snap to whole pixels, so scaled sprites needed my own run-length painter.\n- **Changed in the engine:** none.\n- **One change I'd make:** a documented rule for canvas size with a fixed resolution, and a note that the first frame can run before later scripts load.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n- **Liked most:** the plan's exact names, file layout, test structure and done criteria.\n- **Confusing:** the task and plan ask for far more than one run can build, and the plan names a different model and effort than the task. The task won.\n- **Hardest:** multiplayer integration with the AI Hub harness, which needs the hub's client and a session flow to test.\n- **Would change:** split it into milestones with their own done lines, so a run can finish one and report the rest.\n\nIf you want the goal finished, the next steps are operations 3–6, the missing enemy types, FURY and DYNAMITE, and then co-op and AI Hub. Those are large enough that they should be a separate run."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":277507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"972ca841-0540-4c71-85fe-204eae6bea61","uuid":"9971226d-7252-42a2-8559-33845f99d787","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:12:27.161Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh5U31GFmGR5rpvUBDVx"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The condition is not met. The assistant's own final message says \"the goal's done condition is **not met**\" and lists missing features against TASK.md: multiplayer (no local co-op, no AI Hub integration), only 2 of 6 operations, missing enemy and pickup types (boats, helicopters, tanks, mortars, knife throwers, snipers, dynamite, FURY), and no Mode 7 or rig system use. The condition requires every feature in TASK.md to be implemented with no stubs. The bundled HTML and exit-interview.json do exist and the four sections appear in the final reply, but the feature-completeness requirement fails."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"972ca841-0540-4c71-85fe-204eae6bea61","uuid":"1d8e5cdc-3544-4874-b8de-aff0e3836083","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:12:31.210Z","isSynthetic":true}
