{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh78dEUbfb4thTq8dxDT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The goal's feature condition is still not met. Ops 1–6, co-op, and an AI Hub session all work, and the bundle and exit interview are valid. But several TASK.md requirements are only partly built, and I'm not going to report the build as complete.\n\n**Built this round**\n\n- **Six operations** with the plan's names and order: Radio Hill, Mangrove Run, Palm Village, Powder Keg Depot, The Kennel (night, rain), and Last Flight Out (storm, cargo plane, gunship boss). Each has a boss, and the bot clears all six headless.\n- **Enemies and pickups added:** officer, RPG, knife thrower, grenadier, brute (head ×4), sniper, mortar, paratroopers, skiffs, gunboat, jeep, truck, APC, tank, gunship, shootable projectiles, dynamite crates, and the FURY pickup.\n- **Co-op:** up to four seats, each with its own crosshair, ammo, and score. Pads join from the title and card screens, and mid-operation joins get six magazines and four grenades. The pause menu has a Drop Out item.\n- **AI Hub session:** the bundle includes `session.js` unmodified, with the plan's meta tags. The host runs the battle, and other copies send inputs and draw from snapshots and events. The real harness passes its two-player conformance checks.\n- **Map and cutscenes:** a map between operations, and text cutscenes for the interrogation and the Kennel.\n- **Checks:** `node tests/run.mjs` passes 85 checks, covering rules, all six bot playthroughs, co-op, a two-copy session through an in-process hub, and every scene drawing.\n\n**Still missing or partial against TASK.md**\n\n- **Engine use:** the Mode 7 floor and the engine's rig and animation system are not used. Art is a depth-scaled pixel painter with procedural sprites.\n- **Operation 2:** the river runs sideways. The plan's forward rail is not built.\n- **Bosses:** each has a volley attack and one special, not the plan's full phases and weak points. Examples are the Big Ear gunner respawns, the Warthog stun and civilian crossings, Iron Hog ammo wagons, Major Tusk's charge, and Hyena One's phases.\n- **Enemies:** no truck or APC unloading, no cargo-plane drops, and no side-channel boat spawns.\n- **Cutscenes:** no briefing scene, no takeoff cut, and the endings are text only. The map and cards stand in for the rest.\n- **Multiplayer:** the host is authoritative. Clients apply the latest snapshot with no interpolation and no hit reports, and the awards field is empty. I only ran two copies in the harness.\n- **Voice:** the caption blips are not Animalese.\n- **Engine:** unchanged.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-03 18:50:13\n- Source: Operation Wolf (Taito, 1987)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: shooter, first-person light-gun rail shooter\n- Perspective: first person on a scripted rail, sideways and in depth\n- Tech: my-3D2dge engine 0.85.2 handoff (JavaScript, 480×270 canvas, chip audio); AI Hub client 1.4.0 unmodified; Node vm for tests; Playwright 1.63.0 for screenshots and the harness\n- Art direction: pixel art made in code, depth-scaled, dusk and dawn palettes\n- Animation: procedural (rise and drop from cover, closing rings, recoil); the engine rig system is not used\n- Audio: engine chip synth with SFX and voice blips in code; engine songs\n- Online: AI Hub session, shared world, 1–4 players, host simulates\n- Testing: 85 Node checks, bot playthroughs of all six operations, a two-copy hub session, screenshots, and the AI Hub harness (two players)\n- Research: none of my own; the plan's summary of the source\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- **Issues caught:** about eight in the first build, seven of them in the game. The expansion added more, and the checks and the harness run caught those too.\n- **Critical:** two would have broken the game in a browser: the canvas drawing at 300×150, and a crash on a deep link into attract because the first frame ran before the bot file loaded. A third was a battle-state name collision, found by the test suite.\n- **Most helpful:** the bot playing each operation to its boss headless, and the harness conformance run.\n- **Least helpful:** the stub-buffer draw pass, which only shows that drawing doesn't throw.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- **Liked most:** the scene flow, pause, settings, input presets, the arcade table and initials, and the headless loop.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** the canvas CSS, the first frame running before later scripts load, and hash deep links that only apply on a fresh load.\n- **Built by hand:** the battle rules, the rail and beat generator, telegraph rings, the depth painter, the HUD, the bot, and the session layer.\n- **Hardest:** the API card is long, and the pixel primitives snap to whole pixels.\n- **Changed in the engine:** none.\n- **One change I'd make:** document the canvas-size rule for fixed resolutions, and say the first frame can run before later scripts load.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- **Liked most:** the plan's exact names, files, tests, and done criteria.\n- **Confusing:** the task and plan together ask for far more than one run, and the plan names a different model and effort than the task.\n- **Hardest:** the AI Hub integration and the shared-world snapshot design.\n- **Would change:** split the work into milestones with separate done lines, and mark which items are optional.\n\nThe next milestone is the Mode 7 and rig requirement, then the boss and cutscene details. Say the word and I'll go on, or `/goal clear` if the current build is enough."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2303,"cache_read_input_tokens":462893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2303},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"972ca841-0540-4c71-85fe-204eae6bea61","uuid":"e5b20977-e931-475f-abeb-699dcb504b69","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:34:16.720Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh78crtzprADFDsG9Mc8"}
